{"availability":"available","full":"FlavioImbertDomingos/certadillo","name":"certadillo","description":"Open source PKI and certificate lifecycle management (CLM): issue, track and renew certificates, with a public read-only demo.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T03:17:36Z","updated":"2026-09-24T18:53:57Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://certadillo.com","topics":["certificate-management","clm","pki","python","tls","x509"],"demo":"https://certadillo.com/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T09:23:41.967Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T09:23:41.967Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T09:23:41.967Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T07:21:26.309Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T09:23:41.967Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Certadillo is an open source PKI and certificate lifecycle platform for regulated shops. It runs an internal CA hierarchy, enrolls certificates over REST, ACME, EST, SCEP, CMP and SSH, keeps an inventory of every certificate it issued or found on the network, and tells the owning team before anything expires. Dilly, the armadillo on top, rolls into a ball when something is critical.","It was built as a reference implementation of what a bank's certificate management service needs: one registration authority in front of every protocol, dual control on sensitive operations, CA keys in an HSM, a tamper-evident audit trail, and reports an auditor can use (PCI DSS v4.0 4.2.1.1 inventory, a CycloneDX crypto bill of materials)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FlavioImbertDomingos/certadillo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"59b118e155c7f8a8d7ad1132717c47552b188b4e81f8d88aabe9a7e49ec4addd","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T07:21:26.459Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T07:21:26.459Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Certadillo is an open source PKI and certifi